\name{leaf_annotation_gap}
\alias{leaf_annotation_gap}
\title{
Spacing between leaf annotation groups
}
\description{
Set the spacing between two adjacent leaf annotation groups.
}
\usage{
leaf_annotation_gap(width = 12)
}
\arguments{
\item{width}{One finite nonnegative number in logical pixels, default 12. Zero makes the two annotation groups touch; fractional widths are supported.}
}
\details{
Insert this layer between leaf_annotation_rect() or leaf_annotation_heatmap() calls. It replaces the default 4-pixel spacing only at that boundary, without changing spacing between columns in an annotation. Other layer types do not consume the gap. Consecutive gap layers use the last width. Gaps before the first annotation or after the last annotation have no effect. All seven tree layouts are supported, including every slanted direction. This layer has no legend and does not start Java.
}
\value{
A \code{yytree_layer} value; add it to a plot with \code{+}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{leaf_annotation_rect}}, \code{\link{leaf_annotation_heatmap}}, \code{\link{leaf_labels}}
}
\examples{
categories <- data.frame(name = c("A", "B"), group = c("one", "two"))
values <- matrix(c(1, 2), dimnames = list(c("A", "B"), "score"))
p <- yytree("(A:1,B:1);") + leaf_annotation_rect(categories) +
  leaf_annotation_gap(width = 12) + leaf_annotation_heatmap(values)

}
